\ Mixed known/opaque numeric operands: an unboxed literal or annotated
\ parameter meets an opaque value at an arithmetic or comparison site.
\ These sites must take the polymorphic path in AOT mode; the concrete
\ path's tag check bails on the other numeric type, and an AOT bail
\ aborts the program instead of deopting.
\
\ Every word is called with both a fixnum and a float argument so the
\ freeze-time call-site inference keeps the parameter opaque. Correct
\ output for both argument types proves no bail occurred.

add3: ( x -- y )          [ 3 + ] ;
radd: ( x -- y )          [ 3 swap + ] ;
fadd: ( x -- y )          [ 1.5 + ] ;
sub3: ( x -- y )          [ 3 - ] ;
rsub: ( x -- y )          [ 10 swap - ] ;
mul3: ( x -- y )          [ 3 * ] ;
div2: ( x -- y )          [ 2 / ] ;
mod2: ( x -- y )          [ 2 % ] ;
lt3:  ( x -- b )          [ 3 < ] ;
gt3:  ( x -- b )          [ 3 > ] ;
eq3:  ( x -- b )          [ 3 = ] ;
mixf: ( a: float b -- c ) [ + ] ;

7 add3 .
2.5 add3 .

7 radd .
2.5 radd .

2 fadd .
2.25 fadd .

10 sub3 .
4.5 sub3 .

3 rsub .
2.5 rsub .

4 mul3 .
2.5 mul3 .

6 div2 .
7.0 div2 .

7 mod2 .
7.5 mod2 .

2 lt3 .
2.5 lt3 .
3.5 lt3 .

4 gt3 .
4.5 gt3 .
2.5 gt3 .

3 eq3 .
3.0 eq3 .
2.5 eq3 .

1.5 2 mixf .
1.5 2.5 mixf .
